# Rebuild QuantForge after edits

After any change that affects the desktop app (Rust crates, `apps/desktop`, Tauri commands, UI), **rebuild and reinstall** before telling the user the app is ready:

```bash
cd apps/desktop
pnpm tauri build

osascript -e 'quit app "QuantForge"' 2>/dev/null || true
killall QuantForge 2>/dev/null || true
rm -rf /Applications/QuantForge.app
cp -R ../../target/release/bundle/macos/QuantForge.app /Applications/QuantForge.app
# Bundle path is workspace target/: QuantForge/target/release/bundle/macos/QuantForge.app
open -a QuantForge
```

- Prefer **release** builds (`pnpm tauri build`, no `--debug`) so Discover/eval run ~10× faster than debug.
- Do this at the end of every edit turn that changes the app; do not leave a stale `/Applications/QuantForge.app`.
